course: dictionary
lesson: 448
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning is right. Argentine is one of these words. «In some Argentine towns, capybaras now graze on lawns and golf courses.» Here Argentine is written with a capital A, so it names a place: Argentina, a country in South America.
explain: Look at the clues. Towns and lawns tell you the sentence is about a place, not a feeling or a fish. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A capital letter often tells you a word names a country or a person. An Argentine is a person from Argentina, so «The Argentine team played well» is about people or a team from that country. With a small a, argentine is a rare word for silvery, like silver. It can also name a small silvery sea fish.
fact: Argentine with a capital A means from or to do with Argentina, a country in South America.
fact: An Argentine is a person from Argentina. Argentinian and Argentinean mean the same.
fact: Argentine with a small a is rare and means silvery, like silver.
fact: An argentine is also a small silvery sea fish.
fact: Check the context: capital letters, nearby words and the topic of the sentence tell you which meaning is right.
exercise: «In some Argentine towns, capybaras now graze on lawns.» In this sentence, what does Argentine mean? | A small silvery fish | Very old | Made of silver | *From Argentina, a country in South America
exercise: Maya says, «My cousin is an Argentine who lives in Buenos Aires.» What is an Argentine? | A golf course | *A person from Argentina | A kind of grass | A silvery sea fish
exercise: «The lake shone argentine under the moon.» What does argentine mean here? | Very warm | *Silvery, like silver | A small sea fish | From Argentina
test: The fisherman caught an argentine in the bay. What is an argentine here? | Something very old | *A small silvery sea fish | A person from Argentina | A golf course
test: Which word can also mean a person from Argentina? | Argentic | *Argentinean | Chilean | Brazilian
exam: «The Argentine family cooked beef on the grill.» Which meaning fits best here? | Very old | *From Argentina, a country in South America | A small silvery sea fish | Silvery, like silver
